  "placement": "Book page 100, topic 4.1: কাজ (Work). Next to the definition W = Fs, the unit box (J, জুল) and the push-then-let-go example (work only over s, none over d).",
  "order": 1,
  "maintainers": ["RadeenXALNW"],
  "units": "m",
  "description": "Interactive 3D figure for textbook topic 4.1 (কাজ, Work), page 100. In a house's tiled courtyard (a teal boundary wall, the guard's gate and stool), a realistic person leans on a wooden crate and pushes it s metres with a force F, then lets go; the crate slides d = s/2 more and stops, the book's own example. The orange F arrow shows only while the hands push, the blue s arrow grows with the crate and W = Fs counts up live; over the grey d the force is gone and W stays put. A second example pushes the crate against a brick wall: s = 0, so W = 0 (the book's guard). A small calculator with tap steppers for F (10–100 N) and s (1–4 m) works W = Fs out in J (জুল); a metre tape on the floor lets the test read s off the picture. Five tap questions: where F did work, W from the tape, the wall, F from W, the unit. The person, crate, floor, wall and arrows export as GLB in metres. Offline, in Bangla and English.",
